{"posts":[{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_701","t":"","a":"bennygill","d":"","n":"#701","p":29,"im":["ad470e61dfbc4e17cc98fceff01043b234c64493"],"m":701},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_702","t":"","a":"bennygill","d":"","n":"#702","p":29,"im":["eac7e13536a70aa25de88f78f21663691b189086"],"m":702},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_703","t":"","a":"bennygill","d":"","n":"#703","p":29,"im":["170f5d5329024c4095fe2a6cd2706bacfed4a6fd"],"m":703},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_704","t":"Very nice Benny! Thanks for your postings.","a":"johnnym","d":"","n":"#704","p":29,"im":[],"m":704},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_705","t":"Here is the bigger m15 chart and the m5 chart which I've marked up. Thoughts?\n\nOr on my 2nd chart as we compress back down to untested demand, are we now expecting price to move up through the supply zone above?\n\nUPDATE: This chart answers my question..Tiiiiiimberrrrr!","a":"tradingjedi","d":"","n":"#705","p":29,"im":["0c86c9d6de4321d9a17fff5e92446bf0f12137ee","0cef4924dd688e139bf2aeae01ee1a81cb28bd66","5d6e3ccaacd9c1f8462c2fe33508661691f12272"],"m":705},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_706","t":"Am I right here?","a":"tradingjedi","d":"","n":"#706","p":29,"im":["ac11990c458a7e35135cdaf8ceddbdfda975c815"],"m":706},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_707","t":"Ok this graph is extremely messy, PA is not very smooth at all, but we should be able to analyse and trade in all conditions...\n\nEverytime I start looking at charts I try and ask the question \"Where was the decision made?\" and with this chart it's very difficult to answer that question, however not impossible.\n\nComments to attached chart: 1.RBD formed (large bear pole) ~ Decision that price was to expensive 2. There is a FL, followed with another FL, a DBR (however this is questionable as price didn't rally, it's more a form of CP or indecision) 3. Rally, with a FL ~ DP, and as price progressed up, I am sure there is a DP in the bearish pole on the left that caused the reaction. 4. Points 4 & 5 is where it really gets messy (I am aware of the fact this was due to news NFP) 5. RBD, once again not really a drop, more CP, with a spike up to test a DP at 5. 6. Drop, base and then compression with a rally or liquidity bar into the supply zone 7. RBD formed 8. DB followed by CP 9. CP upwards, consuming the supply, with a few DP 10, Price rallied to 1, tested the previous DP, formed a new RBD ~ DP ~ Supply zone 11. CP down, consuming demand 12. CP however this is more a drop (rally down) 13. DBD, also a FL 14. DB, followed by CP...or probably a large base 15. More CP, testing the base at 14. 16. DBR ~ Decision that price is too cheap","a":"Danish","d":"","n":"#707","p":29,"im":["52249a6e9ae283c51b8a0123cb6ad29b54398b4b"],"m":707},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_708","t":"Anybody know how to print the entire book of compression? thanks!","a":"thestarting","d":"","n":"#708","p":29,"im":[],"m":708},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_709","t":"Hello all,\n\nIt's been a while since I submitted any form of homework, but I have been busy learning nonetheless. I put this one in my journal and thought I'd share it here as well.\n\nPlease excuse the image if it is difficult to view, I've had to resize it to get it past the upload pixie.\n\nRegards.\n\nSpongy.","a":"Spongiform","d":"","n":"#709","p":29,"im":["4add36d0ec66e01032964c8955e6733f38a12009"],"m":709},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_710","t":"looking for complete the homework with CP","a":"Jiris109","d":"","n":"#710","p":29,"im":["20a5a24350a976a62ad8b148ba01f83dec9cf560"],"m":710},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_711","t":"I'm new here. This is by far the best site when it comes to trading. I want to start posting charts but i want to understand things a little better. Does anyone know where i can find the book that's often referred to in this thread?","a":"josh1125","d":"","n":"#711","p":29,"im":[],"m":711},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_712","t":"The only book I know about is there: acegazette.com/en/? option=com_flippingbo...1&Itemid=514&lang=en\n\nChris\n\njosh1125 wrote: I'm new here. This is by far the best site when it comes to trading. I want to start posting charts but i want to understand things a little better. Does anyone know where i can find the book that's often referred to in this thread?","a":"kkb","d":"","n":"#712","p":29,"im":[],"m":712},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_713","t":"here: www.freefilehosting.net/compression anyway is all into the marketpedia:) bye","a":"whiteout","d":"","n":"#713","p":29,"im":[],"m":713},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_714","t":"This important document should be located in our website, So here it is for direct download www.readthemarket.com/media/pdf/Compression.pdf","a":"benhur","d":"","n":"#714","p":29,"im":["991ea1be359743b6730a5d1b458341dd405d7805"],"m":714},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_715","t":"Thank you all for leading me to the compression book. I am very new at this, and hoping to start doing my homework assignments once I feel like I've understood it","a":"josh1125","d":"","n":"#715","p":29,"im":[],"m":715},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_716","t":"there's a big spike, then price resumed its way up. could this be considered as a compression?","a":"azlan1","d":"","n":"#716","p":29,"im":["cc1bf4ebf8f168a2d361c2a443ede99e38e0bbdb"],"m":716},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_717","t":"azlan1 wrote: there's a big spike, then price resumed its way up. could this be considered as a compression?\n\nAsk yourself some questions; In terms of SD consumption, what is the expected reaction when price return to a cp area. then look if the expected action happened. Last, think about the contribution of the reaction formation to the balance of SD. What do you think is happening in your scenario?","a":"benhur","d":"","n":"#717","p":29,"im":["cc1bf4ebf8f168a2d361c2a443ede99e38e0bbdb"],"m":717},{"id":"aboutcompression_p29_718","t":"Hello, here are some charts where I marked some compression zones, would be glad if you can comment them, what I did wrong.","a":"Mike1","d":"","n":"#718","p":29,"im":["ed64